<!--
   Auto Backup rules for API <= 30 (android:fullBackupContent). For API 31+
   see data_extraction_rules.xml. Mirrors the phone's pair of files; the
   rationale (security-audit finding M6, 2026-05-14) is written out there.

   Why the watch has these AT ALL, as of the door snapshot: until then the
   Wear app persisted nothing, so its manifest declared no backup rules and
   the platform default (allowBackup="true", empty rules) had nothing to
   copy. Adding the first on-disk file silently made the watch's door-activity
   history eligible for Google Drive Auto Backup — the exact fail-open the
   phone's guardrail exists to prevent, on a module the guardrail did not
   cover. Both halves are fixed together.

   Path is source-confirmed (so an exclude cannot silently fail open):
   WEAR_STATUS_CACHE_FILE_NAME in WearStatusCacheStorage.kt is resolved
   against context.filesDir, i.e. the "file" backup domain. Enforced by the
   checkWearBackupRulesExcludes Gradle task.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="file" path="wear_status_cache.preferences_pb" />
</full-backup-content>
